        <mxCell id="2bkVFfdwQwM_3sd6mGNa-16" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;" value="We use the same method to add in the additional cycles at the boundaries in NAS.c to generate a maximal NAS, this sequence is also a complement avoiding sequence.&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Then we add one final sequence that uses (0,k/2) instead of binary, and the sequence is added at the end of the NAS sequence. Thus achieving a maximal CAS.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
